    <h4>Purpose of this website</h4>
    <p class="policy-text">OpenCRO publishes product comparisons and cybersecurity, privacy, and business risk analyses of AI-enabled medical devices and related healthcare software.</p>
    <p class="policy-text">Our goal is to educate, inform, and encourage discussion about cybersecurity, privacy, and business risk in digital health while demonstrating the OpenCRO methodology for business threat modeling and risk analysis.</p>

    <h4>Public information only</h4>
    <p class="policy-text">Our analyses are generated using publicly available information, such as OpenFDA, published regulatory submissions, public company websites, product documentation, scientific publications, press releases, and other publicly available sources.</p>
    <ol class="policy-list">
      <li>We do not use confidential company information.</li>
      <li>We do not access private systems.</li>
      <li>We do not claim knowledge of any organization's internal security controls.</li>
    </ol>

    <h4>Modeled Scenarios</h4>
    <p class="policy-text">OpenCRO generates modeled product comparisons, threat stories, threat models, asset valuations, risk scores, and mitigation recommendations using the OpenCRO methodology.</p>
    <p class="policy-text">They describe plausible cybersecurity and privacy scenarios derived from publicly available information and established risk analysis techniques. They are not statements of fact about any organization's actual security posture. The existence of a modeled threat or vulnerability does not imply that such a vulnerability exists in any specific product, device, or organization.</p>

    <h4>Accuracy</h4>
    <p class="policy-text">We aim to use accurate and current public information. However, public information may be incomplete, outdated, or incorrect. If you believe that any page contains a factual error based on publicly available information, we welcome your feedback and will review the material promptly.</p>

    <h4>No professional advice</h4>
    <p class="policy-text">The information on this website is provided for educational and informational purposes only. Nothing on this website should be considered legal, regulatory, cybersecurity, engineering, investment, medical, or other professional advice. Organizations should perform their own independent assessments before making business or technical decisions.</p>

